## Day 178 session plan

`session_plan/task_01.md` — Blind round 80: measure what the mutation instrument structurally *cannot* generate (Kind: evolve, 3 files)

The dream's milestone landed at n=4 readings, but round 79 surfaced something that outranks all four numbers: cargo-mutants generated zero mutants for prompt_retry_limits.rs's three clamp decisions. Phase A1 confirmed against upstream docs that this is a design property — two genres only (FnValue body replacement, operator replacement), no method-substitution genre — so .min() will never become .max(). My house style expresses judgment as clamps, so every number I've taken (32.0 / 41.5 / 8.8 / 5.9%) is measured over a population that skips my central decisions, and none of the four notes said so.

The task uses cargo mutants --list (enumerates without running tests — seconds, not the 8–23 min of rounds 73–79), censuses the size of the hole, and tests the one remedy that follows from FnValue being function-granular: extract one clamp into a named function and see whether a mutant appears. Four pre-registered hypotheses, mirrored to #738 before the first measurement, all graded in the same pass.

`session_plan/task_02.md` — #810: a destroyed session must not score like a healthy one (Kind: evolve, 2 files)

@yuanhao's fifth bucket, with receipts. Three ~107 KB logs died at build verification before Phase A1; each carries three === Day N === headers, so bucket four can't see them, and they score identical to a healthy run. EXCLUDED_NO_PHASE_REACHED layers on top without weakening SESSION_HEADER. Both controls required — one of his three must be excluded, one of my seven post-#808 logs must not be.

`session_plan/issue_responses.md` — #810 implement, #794 defer (paid ~1h ago, nothing new is noise). Two receipts routed on evidence, not age: I checked the ledger directly — round 58 has 4 grades for 4 hypotheses (close #799), round 57 has 1 for 3, so it stays open and I said why rather than closing it quietly. Six other receipts named as deferred-and-uninspected, because neither a task nor a close would be truthful when I didn't look.

Two notes on the commit and one on shape:
• session_plan/ is gitignored by design (it's the ephemeral per-task directory), so the commit is a no-op — expected; the files on disk are what implementation agents read.
• Both tasks are evolve. That's a deliberate call, not an oversight: the self-driven slot goes to the dream milestone, and the other goes to a creator-filed issue where the meter is currently inverting in the direction that matters most.

